    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released in September 1998 by Island Records, Lock, Stock & Two Smoking Barrels – Original Soundtrack is a genre-spanning compilation that mirrors the energy and attitude of Guy Ritchie’s breakout British crime film. The album blends electronic, rock, and funk/soul influences, featuring a mix of classic tracks and contemporary hits. Standout songs include Ocean Colour Scene’s Britpop anthem “Hundred Mile High City,” E-Z Rollers’ drum’n’bass masterpiece “Walk This Land,” and James Brown’s funk staples “The Boss” and “The Payback.” The soundtrack also incorporates memorable dialogue snippets, enhancing its narrative quality and immersing listeners in the film’s gritty, fast-paced world.\n\nMusically, the album is celebrated for its eclectic curation, bridging decades and styles with tracks like The Stooges’ proto-punk “I Wanna Be Your Dog,” Dusty Springfield’s sultry “Spooky,” and Lewis Taylor and Carleen Anderson’s cover of “18 With A Bullet.” This diverse selection not only complements the film’s irreverent tone but also stands as a testament to the era’s vibrant British music scene. Upon its original release, the soundtrack achieved both critical acclaim and commercial success, frequently cited as one of the best movie soundtracks of all time for its bold, genre-defying approach and its role in shaping the identity of modern British gangster cinema.",
